    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t-notes",
      "x": 140, "y": 420,
      "text": "Key facts about the Rialto District:\n- Rialto = 'Rivoalto' (high bank) — the first inhabited area of Venice\n- The wooden Rialto Bridge was the only bridge over the Grand Canal until the Accademia Bridge (1854)\n- The Fondaco dei Tedeschi was the largest of several 'fondachi' (foreign trading compounds)\n- German merchants lived here under strict curfew — locked in at night\n- Dante Gabriel Rossetti's father was a custodian here in the 19th century\n- The Rialto banking district was Europe's first concentration of public and private banks",
      "fontSize": 8, "fontFamily": 1, "strokeColor": "#a0aec0",
      "originalText": "Key facts about the Rialto District:", "autoResize": true
    }
